+## `machines`
+
+Access: capability `machines`.
+
+Capability `machines`, server mods only (manifest `api = "0.3"`, experimental): the slots and screen values of content mods' machines (`data/<ns>/horizon_machine/<block>.json`). The game keeps the slots: it saves them with the chunk, shows them in the machine's screen, where players move items as in a furnace's, and drops them when the block goes. The item record and the slot rules are those of API 0.4's `machine` interface, here addressed by position.
+
+### record `item-stack`
+
+An item, how many, its wear and its custom data. Other item components are not carried: a slot set to the item it holds keeps them.
+
+| Field | Type | |
+| --- | --- | --- |
+| `id` | `string` | `minecraft:coal`, `<mod>:<path>`, ... |
+| `count` | `u32` |  |
+| `damage` | `u32` | `minecraft:damage`: the wear of a tool (a blade), 0 for none. |
+| `custom` | `option<string>` | `minecraft:custom_data` as SNBT (`{ntm_ore:{light:1.5d}}`), as `/give` takes it. Setting none keeps what the slot's same item had; stacks of different custom data don't stack. |
+
+### record `button-press`
+
+A player pressed one of a machine screen's buttons.
+
+| Field | Type | |
+| --- | --- | --- |
+| `player` | `string` | The player's UUID. |
+| `dimension` | `string` |  |
+| `x` | `s32` |  |
+| `y` | `s32` |  |
+| `z` | `s32` |  |
+| `button` | `u32` | The button's number in the screen file. |
+
+| Function | Signature | What it does |
+| --- | --- | --- |
+| `get-slots` | `func(dimension: string, x: s32, y: s32, z: s32) -> option<list<option<item-stack>>>` | The slots of the machine at a position, as of this call: none where there is none, or no chunk is loaded. |
+| `set-slot` | `func(dimension: string, x: s32, y: s32, z: s32, slot: u32, stack: option<item-stack>) -> bool` | Sets one slot (none empties it) after this call returns, before players act again; a stack over the item's maximum is cut to it. False for no machine there, a slot out of range, an unknown item or custom data that isn't an SNBT compound. |
+| `set-data` | `func(dimension: string, x: s32, y: s32, z: s32, values: list<s32>) -> bool` | The values the machine's screen shows (bars, tooltips, lights), from the first: at most the file's `data`, the rest kept. False for no machine there. |
+| `poll-buttons` | `func() -> list<button-press>` | The button presses since the last call, oldest first (at most 256). |
+| `get-data` | `func(dimension: string, x: s32, y: s32, z: s32) -> option<list<s32>>` | The machine's values as last set (saved with the chunk, so a mod keeps there what must not part from the slots), as of this call: none where there is no machine. |
+
 ## `server-events`
 
 Access: exported by the mod: the game calls it.
